WEBVTT

00:11:56.996 --> 00:12:00.556
Dressed in a formal white shirt
and black tails,

00:12:00.596 --> 00:12:02.276
as if for a night at the opera,

00:12:02.476 --> 00:12:04.476
he sat down on a white plastic chair

00:12:04.516 --> 00:12:05.836
on a mound of rubble,

00:12:05.836 --> 00:12:08.156
and he played his cello.

00:12:08.196 --> 00:12:10.956
And he did that every day for 22 days

00:12:10.996 --> 00:12:14.036
under sniper fire that never stopped him.

00:12:15.036 --> 00:12:18.316
"You ask me am I crazy to play my cello
in the middle of a war zone,"

00:12:18.356 --> 00:12:19.636
he said,

00:12:19.636 --> 00:12:22.876
"Why don't you ask them
if they're crazy for shelling Sarajevo?"

00:12:24.356 --> 00:12:25.716
A few months after that,

00:12:25.716 --> 00:12:28.236
the BBC foreign correspondent,
Allan Little, writes

00:12:28.276 --> 00:12:31.436
that he watched as a procession
of 40,000 people